# Downloaded meeting packets — large, and re-fetchable via
# `python3 data/agenda_watch.py --fetch <agendaId>`
briefs/raw/*.pdf
briefs/raw/*.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Cached meeting attachments: keep the pdftotext output, not the PDFs.
# A single meeting runs ~14MB of PDF against ~0.6MB of text, and at two
# meetings a week that is ~1.5GB/year in git. The .txt is what gets read and
# quoted; every brief records the source URL, so the PDF is re-fetchable.
# This is a deliberate deviation from the parent repo's "cache every primary
# source" rule, made for repo size. The PDFs still sit on disk locally.
# Widened 2 Sep 2026: the old pattern only matched folders named exactly
# YYYY-MM-DD, so a folder named 2026-09-08-pc or comp-plan slipped through and
# a 9.5MB agenda packet was staged. Any per-meeting cache folder now matches.
data/*/*/*.pdf
